// csPrepend is SHARED as rtPrepend - lib/runtime.metajs.

// ----- method-group conversion (docs/todo.md 1.1) -----
// ECMA-334 10.8 makes a method group convertible to a compatible delegate type, and
// 20.1 gives the delegate the receiver the group was formed on as its target; 20.5
// makes two delegates equal when target and method are equal, which here (delegates
// are compared by object identity) means the bound closure has to be MEMOISED - one
// object per (receiver, method) - or `E -= s.Got` would not remove what
// `E += s.Got` added.
//
// The EMITTER builds the forwarder (a parameterless closure that captures the
// receiver in a scope of its own and re-enters through js_mcall) because layer 2
// cannot: MetaJS has no `arguments` and no rest parameter, so a closure written here
// would have to fix an arity, and the target method's arity is not known at the
// conversion site. This decides only WHICH object the group denotes.
//
// The twins are csMethodGroup in languages/csharp-interpreter.abnf and js_csmg in
// abnf/jsrtcsharp.go. `__mg_` is a `__`-prefixed slot, so keysOf hides it from every
// clone, record equality and struct copy (manual 7.9).
function js_csmg(recv, name, bound) {
    if (recv === undefined || recv === null) { return undefined }
    if (typeof recv != "object") { return undefined }
    if (recv["__isclass"] === true) {
